#
# WirelessManager (wpa_supplicant) configuration.
#
# C:WirelessManager reads ENV:Sys/Wireless.prefs unless CONFIG says otherwise
# (workbench/network/WirelessManager/wpa_supplicant/main_amiga.c). If the file
# is absent it stops at "Failed to read or parse configuration" before its MUI
# window is ever created -- so a machine that has never configured a network
# cannot reach the scanner that would configure one. This file exists to break
# that circle, and ships with no network blocks on purpose: a configuration
# with nothing to associate to is a valid configuration.
#
# Scan and Connect in the WirelessManager window work from here. What they add
# does not come back to this file: wpa_supplicant is built with
# CONFIG_NO_CONFIG_WRITE=y and cannot write its own configuration at all.
# Prefs/Network is what persists networks, into ENVARC:Sys and ENV:Sys both
# (workbench/prefs/network/prefsdata.c, WriteWirelessPrefs).
#
# A network looks like this, in the form Prefs/Network writes:
#
#   network={
#       ssid="my network"
#       psk="my passphrase"
#       key_mgmt=WPA-PSK
#   }
#
